course: dictionary
lesson: 2653
title: Detox: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Detox is a good example. In a hospital, a detox is real medical help for someone stopping a drug or alcohol. Outside hospital, people use the word more loosely, for a break from something or a healthy eating plan.
explain: «Your liver and kidneys remove waste from your body every day; detox teas don't have good evidence behind them.» The sentence tells you the body already cleans itself, so detox teas are not the magic cleaners some adverts claim. Good evidence means proof from careful tests. When a claim sounds too good, check the clues before you believe it.
explain: Detox also appears in phrases. A «digital detox» is a break from phones and screens, which can help you sleep and feel better. A «detox diet» is a short spell of eating only certain foods. Ask yourself: what is being cleaned, and who says so? Then use the context to decide which meaning fits.
fact: In a hospital, a detox means medical help when a person stops taking a drug or alcohol.
fact: In everyday talk, a detox can mean a time of eating only healthy food.
fact: A «digital detox» is a break from phones and screens.
fact: Your liver and kidneys already clean your blood and remove waste every day.
fact: «Detox diets» and «detox teas» are mostly a myth, because there is little good evidence that they work.
exercise: «Your liver and kidneys remove waste from your body every day.» What do the liver and kidneys do? | *They clean waste out of the body | They make you grow taller | They keep your eyes moist | They help you hear
exercise: «A digital detox» means what? | A new phone with a longer battery | *A break from phones and screens | A plate of green vegetables | A visit to the doctor for a check-up
exercise: A friend says detox means a special treatment in hospital. In a hospital, what does detox mean? | A special drink that cleans your blood | *Medical help to stop taking a drug or alcohol | A fast run around the park | A plan for a school trip
test: «Detox teas don't have good evidence behind them.» What does this sentence suggest about detox teas? | They are proven to make you healthy | They are only for doctors | They are the best way to clean your body | *They have not been shown to work well
test: Which word in «Your liver and kidneys remove waste from your body every day» means get rid of something? | every | liver | *remove | kidneys
exam: Mia says detox teas will clean her body for ever. What does the sentence «Detox teas don't have good evidence behind them» tell us? | Mia's liver is broken | *Detox teas have not been shown to work, so her claim is doubtful | Detox teas are proven to clean the body | Detox teas are only for doctors
